    Derive the stage mask capacity and the random tail
    
    The trusted planner now derives a middle stage's mask capacity and a last
    stage's single-row capacity from the previous stage: the folded row is cut
    into two-to-the-k rows after a divisibility check, the mask length is the
    power of two that holds the carried entries, the samples and the pad, the
    out-of-domain entries are what remains, and the row's random tail follows the
    position count with the domain's parity rule. Unit tests cover the middle and
    last stages, an indivisible cut and the parity rule.
    
    This is the second piece of the sizing derivation; the configuration
    candidates, the stage lists, the joint shared and own solve, the capacity
    mapping and the full round budget remain the next steps.

